    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Charming countryside traditional home exuding character and charm both inside and out. \nThis special property was a jewel in the crown of the bustling and close knit community for many years, serving as a small shop\n\nLovingly renovated and enhanced by its attentive owners this 3 bedr. property with generous living space, blends period character with contemporary comfort. \n\nSituated in a picturesque courtryside setting, the property sits on a wonderfully kept c. 0.5 acres complemented by stunning mature trees, shrubs and flowering plants. \n\nThis picture perfect country property is a 12 minute drive to Clonakilty, c. 5 minutes drive to Knockskeagh National school and Co op Shop/Hardware store.\n\n\nCharming countryside traditional home exuding character and charm both inside and out. \nThis special property was a jewel in the crown of the bustling and close knit community for many years, serving as a small shop and filling station.\n\nLovingly renovated and enhanced by its attentive owners this 3 bedr. property with generous living space, blends period character with contempory comfort. \n\nSituated in a picturesque courtryside setting, the property sits on a wonderfully kept c. 0.5 acres complemented by stunning mature trees, shrubs and flowering plants. \n\nThis picture perfect country property is a 12 minute drive to Clonakilty, c. 5 minutes drive to Knockskeagh National school and Co op Shop/Hardware store.\n\n\nAccommodation c. 101 m²/1087 ft² \n\nReception/Old Shop 4.1 m x 3.8 m\nCharming entrance leads to a bright, spacious, south facing room which was the original shop complete with counter and shelving. Pannelled ceiling and concrete floor.\n\nBack Kitchen 4.1 m x 3.6 m\nA large window makes this a bright and airy room. There are fitted kitchen units and ample storage. The room has a solid fuel stove. Tiled flooring and door to kitchen.\n\nKitchen 3.5 m x 3 m & 3.5 m x 1 m \nStylishly appointed, this beautiful kitchen boasts panoramic coutryside views and is a wonderful blend of the traditional and contemporary. There are fitted units, an integated hob, oven and Belfast sink and ample chic shelving. Timber flooring and doors leading to the bathroom and a sitting room.\n\nBathroom 1.7 m x 2.5 m \nElegantly appointed bathroom with Bath, WC and WHB. The bathroom has both characterful wall panelling and tiling. \n\nSitting Room 3.2 m x 4 m\nCharacterful lounge with an open fire. Carpeted throughout with door leading to a office/study and the beautiful original staircase leading to the first floor.\n\nOffice/Study/Bedroom Three 1.9 m x 3.1 m \nBright and comfortable office/study. Carpeted throughout\n\nCarpeted stairs to first floor landing\n\nBedroom One 3.7 m x 2.2 m \nDouble bedroom carpeted throughout, boasting lovely garden views.\n\nBedroom Two 3.7 m x 2.3 m \nDouble bedroom carpeted throughout, boasting lovely garden views.\n\nServices\nThere is a private well and septic tank. Broadband is available, Imagine Broadband is currently installed. \nHeating is by means of oil fired central heating, a stove in the back kitchen and an open fire in the sitting room. \n\nOutside\nThere is a large concrete built outbuilding together with a timber shed.\n\nDirections: \nType Eircode P85 VX25 into smart phone for exact driving directions. \n\n\n"
      },
